content.text:
Re-audit verdict: **FAIL for “fully implemented, all phases.”** The implementation is substantially improved and locally robust, but four high-severity blockers remain.

- Provider-neutral core embeds Cloudflare MX records.
- Inbound deduplication uses sender-controlled `Message-ID` or a random ID, risking duplicates or silent message collapse.
- CLI `--json` bypasses redaction and exposes credentials/content.
- Real Cloudflare delivery, actual Router/unrelated consumers, restore rehearsal, and seven-day rollout thresholds remain unverified.

Additional issues include non-conformant MCP notification handling, unrecoverable stale SendFn transactions, pre-validation raw buffering, unbounded ingress-reservation growth, and incomplete SendFn CI coverage.

Coverage:

- SFN-17 acceptance: **2 PASS, 4 PARTIAL**
- Technical specification: **28 PASS, 5 PARTIAL, 3 FAIL**
- Verification: **81 MailFn tests + 44 SendFn tests passed**, workerd D1/R2/Email/Queue passed, migration and pack/install/import gate passed.

Comparable-product verdict: MailFn is approaching parity for selected self-hosted mailbox primitives—disposable inboxes, waits, extraction, attachments, threads, drafts, webhooks, and scoped access. It is **not product-comparable** with MailSlurp’s broader hosted testing/protocol platform, [Mailtrap’s hosted inboxes, routing, folders and analytics](https://mailtrap.io/inbound-email/), or [AgentMail’s hosted agent inboxes, WebSockets, SDK breadth and MCP](https://docs.agentmail.to/knowledge-base/inbox-capabilities). [MailSlurp’s inbox and protocol surface](https://www.mailslurp.com/docs/inboxes/) is also materially broader.

Full report: [2026-08-11-9f087abf-full-audit.md](/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/mailfn/.conduct/audits/2026-08-11-9f087abf-full-audit.md)

::code-comment{title="[P1] Cloudflare policy leaks into core" body="The provider-neutral core constructs Cloudflare-specific MX records. Move provider DNS requirements behind MailFnDomainAdapter or runtime configuration so another inbound provider can implement custom domains without modifying core." file="/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/mailfn/mailfn/core/src/service.ts" start=1262 end=1267 priority=1}

::code-comment{title="[P1] Delivery identity is not stable" body="RFC Message-ID is sender-controlled and may be absent; the random fallback also changes on every retry. This can collapse distinct messages or duplicate a retried delivery. Supply or derive a stable runtime delivery key and test both cases." file="/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/mailfn/mailfn/cloudflare/src/worker.ts" start=110 end=112 priority=1}

::code-comment{title="[P1] JSON output bypasses redaction" body="The JSON branch emits raw API data without redactForCommand, exposing one-time credentials and message content without --show-content. Apply the same command-aware sanitizer before selecting the output format." file="/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/mailfn/mailfn/cli/src/index.ts" start=21 end=23 priority=1}

::code-comment{title="[P2] MCP replies to notifications" body="Unknown JSON-RPC notifications reach method-not-found handling and receive an id:null response, which JSON-RPC prohibits. Treat every request without an id as a notification and never write a response." file="/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/mailfn/mailfn/mcp/src/server.ts" start=69 end=71 priority=2}

::code-comment{title="[P2] Pending transaction cannot be reclaimed" body="After the reclaim timeout, inserting the same deterministic primary key fails and the catch returns the existing pending transaction. Use a conditional lease/update so crash recovery neither resends blindly nor remains pending forever." file="/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/mailfn/sendfn/typescript/src/email/service.ts" start=45 end=77 priority=2}

::code-comment{title="[P2] Raw stream is buffered before validation" body="The complete email body is consumed before recipient, status, size, sender-policy and quota validation. Perform the cheap envelope/rawSize checks and reservations first to avoid unnecessary memory work for rejected mail." file="/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/mailfn/mailfn/cloudflare/src/worker.ts" start=106 end=118 priority=2}

::code-comment{title="[P2] Hourly quota ledger grows forever" body="Accepted ingress reservations are retained permanently; only failed ingress releases them. Add scheduled or reservation-time cleanup for expired buckets so the durable table and indexes remain bounded." file="/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/mailfn/mailfn/cloudflare/src/d1-store.ts" start=348 end=376 priority=2}

